WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Thursday,

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.520
the twenty-ninth of October.

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.400
This episode is written with AI,
and read by an AI clone of my voice.

4
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.840
Qatar's halt on liquefied
natural gas, or LNG,

5
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.000
now runs to the end of the year,
which means Europe and Asia head into

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.640
winter without Qatari term cargoes.

7
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.480
And the first Russian diesel cargo
bound for the US has dropped New York

8
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.400
as its destination, after
lawmakers threatened legal action.

9
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.400
On the markets. European gas has
climbed to its highest level since the

10
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.840
autumn of twenty twenty-two,
OilPrice dot com reported.

11
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.480
EU storage stood at seventy-five
percent full on Tuesday,

12
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.160
barely changed on the day, according
to Gas Infrastructure Europe.

13
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.320
In the week to the
twenty-third of October,

14
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.400
US commercial crude stocks fell by
about one point nine million barrels,

15
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.240
according to the EIA. And Scorpio
Tankers says its Long Range Two product

16
00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.840
tankers are booking an average of about
one hundred and eighty-one thousand

17
00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.160
dollars a day.

18
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.440
Starting with Qatar. QatarEnergy has
told Italy's Edison that the force

19
00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.227
majeure in place since April now
runs until the end of December,

20
00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:10.667
according to Edison. That
confirmation comes from a buyer.

21
00:01:10.693 --> 00:01:13.680
There's no statement from QatarEnergy
itself in the reports we've seen

22
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.693
today, and no figure for
the volumes affected.

23
00:01:16.747 --> 00:01:19.080
With term cargoes gone
for the rest of the year,

24
00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.960
buyers are left fighting over spot
LNG, and Europe is doing that with

25
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.320
stocks still building only slowly.

26
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.800
India shows the strain on the Asian side.

27
00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.040
Qatar supplied about forty-five
percent of its LNG imports last year,

28
00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:35.600
and the country is now heading for
record October imports at prices that

29
00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.240
have tripled in a year.

30
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.147
Refiners could feel it too.

31
00:01:39.173 --> 00:01:42.040
Dearer gas raises their
fuel and hydrogen costs,

32
00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.533
and could push some users
toward oil products,

33
00:01:44.587 --> 00:01:46.920
which would firm diesel and fuel oil.

34
00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:51.360
Now the diesel tanker. The Malta-flagged
Agioi Fanendes left Primorsk

35
00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.200
on the twenty-second with about forty
thousand tonnes of ultra-low sulphur

36
00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.760
diesel. It was due in New York
on the seventh of November.

37
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.480
Lloyd's List had it idling
off Skagen on Monday,

38
00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.720
and its tracking now reads "for
orders", meaning no declared port.

39
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.080
The change follows a letter on
Tuesday from Senator Blumenthal,

40
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:12.560
who told the owner that delivering
the cargo would breach federal law

41
00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.080
and asked for the ship to turn
around, gCaptain reported.

42
00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:20.640
A bipartisan group of lawmakers has also
warned US banks and port authorities

43
00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.680
that handling Russian diesel could
bring civil and criminal liability.

44
00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.640
So the legal risk now sits with anyone
who would receive or finance the

45
00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:29.760
cargo.

46
00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.680
Moscow tells it differently.

47
00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.760
According to Alexander Novak, three
cargoes are underway and a fourth

48
00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.600
was due to sail yesterday.

49
00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.000
The US has not confirmed that.

50
00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.640
Separately, a note from UBS puts Russian
oil exports only about ten percent

51
00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.560
below pre-war levels.

52
00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.040
To the Gulf. The US military has told
vessels with no need to move between

53
00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.080
Gulf of Oman and Hormuz
ports to stay away,

54
00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.160
Bloomberg reported. At least fifty
tankers are stuck in the Gulf.

55
00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:02.480
Iran's Persian Gulf Strait Authority
now says sweeping action against

56
00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:06.480
the fleet of Sinokor, the largest
owner of very large crude carriers,

57
00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.480
will begin on the first of November.

58
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.200
Rigzone describes it as legal action.

59
00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.880
That is Iran's claim only,
and nothing has been done yet.

60
00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.400
Oil rose on Wednesday on a
report of an Iranian attack,

61
00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.920
though no price figure was given.

62
00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.320
ING says traders are positioning
for renewed hostilities after the US

63
00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.880
midterms, and expects prices to
fall if no escalation follows.

64
00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:33.280
On the diplomatic track, Saudi,
Turkish and Pakistani delegations met

65
00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.000
Iranian officials in Tehran on Monday.

66
00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:40.160
Tehran wants US sanctions and the port
blockade dealt with before broader

67
00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.120
talks.

68
00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.000
Over in China, refiners are paying up.

69
00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:48.160
As of a Kpler note on the twenty-first,
Iranian oil on water outside

70
00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.880
the blockade zone had fallen to zero.

71
00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:55.360
Kpler sees Iran's oil revenue on
course to vanish by mid-December.

72
00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.800
With those barrels gone and more
competition for Russian crude,

73
00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.640
Chinese refiners are buying West African
and Brazilian grades for December

74
00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.720
delivery, Bloomberg reported.

75
00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:08.080
They're paying premiums of up to
twenty dollars a barrel over Brent on

76
00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.960
the Intercontinental Exchange.

77
00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:13.120
Easier freight over the
past two weeks has helped.

78
00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.440
Formerly sanctioned ships
are moving in as well.

79
00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.000
Two very large crude carriers that
once hauled Venezuelan crude are now

80
00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.520
lifting Gulf oil, and two more
are heading to the Gulf of Oman.

81
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.680
On Gulf supply, the readings don't agree.

82
00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:30.880
Ship-tracking data reported by Rigzone
show Saudi exports holding near

83
00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.600
wartime highs this month,
despite the attacks.

84
00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.080
According to Kpler, Basrah exports
are rebounding toward three million

85
00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.000
barrels a day in October.

86
00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:44.960
UBS takes the other side, saying Gulf
flows remain below prewar levels.

87
00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.800
It raised its end-of-year Brent
forecast to one hundred and ten dollars,

88
00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:52.960
up from one hundred. Its curve for
next year starts at ninety-five dollars

89
00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:56.600
in March. From there it
steps down to ninety by June,

90
00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.400
and eighty-five by September.

91
00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.400
Shipowners are the clear winners.

92
00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.760
Bahri's net profit rose
tenfold in the third quarter.

93
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:07.280
It came to nearly one
point four billion dollars.

94
00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.440
Back to US inventories, with the
full EIA numbers for the week to the

95
00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:16.000
twenty-third. Crude now sits four
percent below the five-year average.

96
00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.080
Two weeks earlier it
was three percent above.

97
00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.720
Distillate stocks fell about
one point five million barrels,

98
00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.640
to just under one hundred
and three million.

99
00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.880
Gasoline went the other way, up nearly
three point nine million barrels

100
00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:30.640
to about two hundred and nine million.

101
00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.240
Refinery utilisation slipped
six tenths of a point,

102
00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.400
